mfl_video_ffmpeg.dll + FFmpeg DLLs - third-party source and licence record
==========================================================================

Upstream
  FFmpeg 7.1  (release tarball, not a git snapshot; git tag n7.1, https://git.ffmpeg.org/gitweb/ffmpeg.git/tag/refs/tags/n7.1)
  URL     https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-7.1.tar.xz
  sha256  40973d44970dbc83ef302b0609f2e74982be2d85916dd2ee7472d30678a7abe6   (checked by build_ffmpeg.sh before every build)
  (upstream detached signature: https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-7.1.tar.xz.asc)
  The tarball is downloaded into tools/video/work/upstream/ at build time (CI: the same URL and sha256). Neither the upstream sources
  nor any binary are stored in this repo.

Movies it must play (the game's toastart/pc/movies, checked with ffprobe 2026-11-20)
  all MPEG-1 video + MPEG-1 Layer II audio: Backdrop/empire/frontend/intro/small/supersonic.mpg = MPEG program stream (mpegps),
  renderware.mpg = raw MPEG-1 video elementary stream (mpegvideo, no audio). Audio 32 / 44.1 / 48 kHz stereo.

configure flags (build_ffmpeg.sh)
  --disable-everything --disable-programs --disable-doc --disable-network --disable-autodetect --disable-asm
  --disable-debug --disable-avdevice --disable-avfilter --disable-swresample --disable-postproc
  --disable-pthreads --disable-w32threads --disable-os2threads
  --enable-protocol=file --enable-demuxer=mpegps,mpegvideo --enable-parser=mpegvideo,mpegaudio
  --enable-decoder=mpeg1video,mp2 --enable-swscale
  win32 target (shipped) adds: --enable-cross-compile --arch=x86 --target-os=mingw32 --cross-prefix=i686-w64-mingw32-
       --enable-shared --disable-static --windres=none --extra-ldflags=-static-libgcc --extra-ldflags=-Wl,--no-insert-timestamp
  native target adds: --enable-pic --enable-static --disable-shared (offline test harness only, not shipped)
  NOT given: --enable-gpl, --enable-version3, --enable-nonfree, any external library (--enable-libx264 etc.); postproc (GPL) disabled.
  configure prints "License: LGPL version 2.1 or later"; build_ffmpeg.sh refuses to continue if it does not.

Our code in this directory
  src/mfl_video_ffmpeg.c   backend glue (calls FFmpeg through its public API), src/harness.c test harness: project code.

LGPL notes (FFmpeg is LGPL 2.1 or later in this configuration)
  * Built LGPL-only: no GPL component is enabled.
  * Layout (W16 VIDCI): FFmpeg is SHARED: avformat-61.dll avcodec-61.dll avutil-59.dll swscale-8.dll, unmodified FFmpeg built by
    build_ffmpeg.sh. mfl_video_ffmpeg.dll (our glue + miniaudio, public domain / MIT-0) links them dynamically through their import libs,
    and the game exe loads mfl_video_ffmpeg.dll at run time with LoadLibrary (recomp/video/mfl_video_null.c); the exe contains no
    FFmpeg code. The user can replace the FFmpeg DLLs with their own build of the same major versions (LGPL 2.1 section 6(b)).
    Without mfl_video_ffmpeg.dll the exe uses the blank video backend (no movies, no menu music).
  * The release zip ships LICENSES/ffmpeg.txt (third_party/LICENSES/ffmpeg.txt): the notice, version, URL, sha256, configure line
    and the full LGPL 2.1 text. The corresponding source is the unmodified upstream tarball above plus these scripts (public repo).
  * FFmpeg is used unmodified (no patches applied to the tarball).
  * Patent/codec note (not a licence matter): only MPEG-1 video and MPEG-1 Layer II audio decoders are compiled in.
  * No binary (DLL, harness, import lib, static libs) is ever committed to this repo; tools/video/work/ is a build directory and must stay untracked.
